3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
 And I'm going to walk you through the process of how I set up my different types of lightning to achieve what I think is a satisfying look.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
 So a bit quick here, I use Cycles.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
 So right now I have zero lights on, so you can't see anything.

6
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:34,000
 And to my left I have the camera view. Here I have the scene view.

7
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:36,000
 And here are my different groups.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
 As you can see I have disabled the lightning for now and the camera.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:43,000
 And here I have all the stuff.

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:45,000
 So yeah.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
 The first thing I'm going to do is to go to the world shader tab.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
 And I have this setup here.

13
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
 And I have another video on my Patreon where I show you how I do this setup.

14
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
 Actually, but a bit fast here.

15
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
 I can show you that I have the sky setup which controls the sky background.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,000
 Go into mix shader.

17
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:11,000
 And then I have an HDRI here which is going to give all the lightning.

18
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
 And then I have a light path in camera array to combine the lightning with the sky background.

19
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
 As you can see the background strength from the HDRI is set to zero.

20
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
 And we can try to set it to one.

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,000
 One is its default value which means that we have the default amount of light coming from the HDRI into the scene.

22
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:36,000
 And as you can see we get some pretty cool results right away.

23
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:41,000
 But in my opinion the lightning here looks a bit dull.

24
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
 It's not really giving much life to the mesh and the structure in the scene.

25
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:51,000
 You can see it's not really that interesting reflections and everything looks like flat almost.

26
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:56,000
 So that's why I often want to add more lightning and not only use an HDRI.

27
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:03,000
 So what I usually do here is that I set the strength of the HDRI texture to maybe 0.5 or 0.7.

28
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
 Maybe we can go to 0.7 here I think.

29
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:11,000
 And you can see now it looks really dull and not really that nice at all.

30
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:19,000
 But I find it that around 0.7 or 0.5 gives me a good foundation to add more lightning on.

31
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
 Without overexposureing it with light.

32
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:26,000
 So the next thing we can do is to activate the light group here.

33
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
 And the first thing I want to show you is the sun.

34
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
 So I'm gonna activate the sun or you can see where I have placed it.

35
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,000
 So the sun is over here and you can see if I disable it.

36
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
